          {
            "definition": {
              "background_color": "gray",
              "content": "**What counts as a deploy here — and what doesn't.**\n\nThese tiles count *GitHub Actions workflow runs that ship something*. All 11 repos are enabled in CI Visibility as of 2026-09-01 (RC1-352).\n\n| Path | Ships | Trigger | Counted |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Fly Deploy` — tpm-automation-platform, pr_agent, launch-planner-agent | Fly apps `tpm-drift-detector`, `pr-review-agent-snacksnack`, `launch-planner-agent` | push to `main` | ✅ all three since RC1-353 |\n| `pages-build-deployment` — agent-evals | GitHub Pages eval site | push to `gh-pages` | ✅ |\n| `Deploy` — ai-incident-summarizer | **incidents.hihelloreid.com** (AWS) | push to `main` | ✅ since RC1-352 |\n| `Deploy` — stale-ticket-bot | AWS CloudFormation stack | push to `main` | ✅ enabled, unverified — dormant since 2026-04-29 |\n| `Heroku Release` — reid_basic | **www.hihelloreid.com** (Heroku) | push to `main`, after CI passes | ✅ since RC1-354 |\n\n**www.hihelloreid.com deploys from Actions since RC1-354** (Heroku auto-deploy is off — it deadlocked with a reporter check; see the ticket). Its deploy shows in these tiles as `Heroku Release` *and* as a DORA event in the group below.\n\nA commit is not a deploy: feature-branch pushes run CI only.\n\nA deploy that succeeds then crash-loops on boot now **fails its workflow** (RC1-355 boot-health gate) and pages via *Fly Deploy failed*. Deploy *frequency/lead-time* live in the **DORA group below** — a different data source these tiles do not query.",
              "font_size": "12",
              "has_padding": true,
              "show_tick": false,
              "text_align": "left",
              "tick_edge": "left",
              "tick_pos": "50%",
              "type": "note",
              "vertical_align": "top"
            },
            "id": 3465254444624968,
            "layout": {
              "height": 5,
              "width": 12,
              "x": 0,
              "y": 5
            }
          }
        ]
