    {
      "definition": {
        "layout_type": "ordered",
        "show_title": true,
        "title": "Security posture — GitHub scanners (RC1-359)",
        "type": "group",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "definition": {
              "background_color": "gray",
              "content": "**Open alerts from GitHub's free scanners — CodeQL, secret scanning — on the five repos, read once a day.** Source is the platform's `Security posture` workflow (`python -m kpi.security_posture`, 11:41 UTC), not Datadog's GitHub telemetry: that collector is organization-scoped and never produced a point for this personal account (RC1-359). One point per day, so the tiles pin a 1-week span — a short window shows *no data*, which is cadence, not an outage. Triage happens in each repo's Security tab; nothing here posts to PRs.",
              "font_size": "14",
              "has_padding": true,
              "show_tick": false,
              "text_align": "left",
              "type": "note",
              "vertical_align": "top"
            },
